#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111842 :tutorial/content "An angle **bisector** is a line that divides an angle into two equal parts.\n\nFor example, in the diagram below, $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{AC}$ is the bisector of the angle $\\angle BAD$.\n\n![](images/3b/3bf65e915f4fc26b8d87199f46ea0bc514195d857890983d31aa2d73eb38a811.png)\n\nThe resulting angles $\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle CAD$ are congruent (they have the same measure)." :tutorial/id #uuid "525bd6d2-3c4c-53fb-aaa5-dab5eee2cf13" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2190 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
